WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.612
- So Starbucks came out with
this Smoked Butterscotch Latte,

00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:04.027
and everybody on the internet is saying

00:00:04.027 --> 00:00:05.432
that it's basically Butterbeer.

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:07.627
So we're gonna try it and
figure out if that's true.

00:00:07.627 --> 00:00:09.054
(whoosh)

00:00:09.054 --> 00:00:13.821
(spooky music)

00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:16.926
- I'm not a fan of Harry Potter.

00:00:16.926 --> 00:00:19.352
- I love everything Harry Potter!

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.873
- I am a Potterhead.

00:00:21.873 --> 00:00:24.626
- Harry Potter is literally life.

00:00:24.626 --> 00:00:27.609
- If one more person or
book wants to convince me

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:30.326
that the "chosen one"
is some basic white guy,

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:32.208
I'm gonna slap them across the face.

00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:33.392
(lightning snap)

00:00:33.392 --> 00:00:35.578
(playful music)

00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:38.873
- Butterbeer is a beer from
Hogwarts, I'm assuming.

00:00:38.873 --> 00:00:43.274
- It's like butterscotch
and a little bit of heaven.

00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:44.969
- I have tried the actual Butterbeer

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:46.536
at the Wizard World of Harry Potter.

00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:48.393
- Is Butterbeer like a Harry Potter thing?

00:00:48.393 --> 00:00:50.089
I so don't know what Butterbeer is.

00:00:50.089 --> 00:00:51.893
What is it?
- Sweet Jesus.

00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:54.436
- This is gonna change your life.

00:00:54.436 --> 00:00:56.011
You're gonna read the books after this.

00:00:56.011 --> 00:00:57.347
- It looks like something from Starbucks.

00:00:57.347 --> 00:00:58.174
- Yeah.

00:00:58.174 --> 00:01:00.193
- Cheers.
- Cheers to terribleness.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.772
- Butterbeer and greatness.
- To grossness.

00:01:01.772 --> 00:01:04.292
- Childhood.
- And badness.

00:01:04.292 --> 00:01:06.172
- Okay, this already doesn't
smell like Butterbeer.

00:01:06.172 --> 00:01:08.228
- It's got that, like,
butterscotchy flavor,

00:01:08.228 --> 00:01:11.000
so I can see why people would
say it's like Butterbeer.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:14.278
- This is nothing like the
Butterbeer that I tried

00:01:14.278 --> 00:01:15.788
at Harry Potter World.

00:01:15.788 --> 00:01:17.495
- It just tastes like butterscotch.

00:01:17.495 --> 00:01:19.573
- Okay, so this isn't quite Butterbeer

00:01:19.573 --> 00:01:20.954
from the Wizarding World of Harry Potter,

00:01:20.954 --> 00:01:22.950
which I think is the closest
that you can get to the book,

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.377
but I do like this drink.

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:26.968
- It's like candy, it's great.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.753
- I think this is as
disappointing as Harry Potter,

00:01:29.753 --> 00:01:31.994
so it's consistent with the legacy.

00:01:31.994 --> 00:01:33.874
- I curse you with my spells.

00:01:33.874 --> 00:01:35.673
It's more about just, like,

00:01:35.673 --> 00:01:37.532
imposing the fandom onto the drink.

00:01:37.532 --> 00:01:39.754
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:39.754 --> 00:01:41.763
(squeaking)

